cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mdis2vihi: pixel-wise spectral reconstruction of a VIHI-like hyperspectral mosaic of Mercury from MESSENGER/MDIS"
message: "If you use this software, the trained model or the synthetic mosaic, please cite this work and the underlying datasets (see docs/DATA.md)."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Müller
    given-names: Raphaël
    affiliation: "LIRA, Laboratoire d'Instrumentation et de Recherche en Astrophysique, Observatoire de Paris, PSL"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-06-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/raphael-muller/mdis2vihi"
keywords:
  - Mercury
  - hyperspectral
  - spectral super-resolution
  - MESSENGER
  - MDIS
  - MASCS
  - VIRS
  - BepiColombo
  - SIMBIO-SYS
  - VIHI
  - planetary science
  - machine learning
abstract: >-
  A fully-connected neural network maps, at a single pixel, the 8-band MDIS
  multispectral reflectance of Mercury (plus the mosaic's image-set count) to a
  231-band VIHI-like spectrum on a common 5 nm grid spanning 300-1450 nm. Trained
  on 153 214 co-located MDIS/MASCS-VIRS pairs with a group split on observation
  identifier, it is applied pixel by pixel over the MESSENGER/MDIS global mosaic
  to produce a synthetic hyperspectral mosaic of the whole planet, intended as an
  early stand-in for BepiColombo/SIMBIO-SYS VIHI data. A second form of the mosaic
  adds a detachable rank-2 correction layer that restores the brightness contrast of
  catalogued hollows, the one surface unit the quality filter excludes from training.
  The repository contains the full pipeline (colocation, target construction,
  training, tiled inference, evaluation), the delivered checkpoint, the correction
  layer and the audit artefacts.
